public class Solution {
    public int subarraySum(int[] nums, int k) {
        int count = 0;
      
        int[] sum = new int[nums.length + 1];
        sum[0] = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i <= nums.length; i++)
            sum[i] = sum[i - 1] + nums[i - 1];
      
        for (int start = 0; start < sum.length; start++) {
            for (int end = start + 1; end < sum.length; end++) {
                if (sum[end] - sum[start] == k)
                    count++;
            }
        }
      
        return count;
    }
}

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** O(n)
- **Space Complexity:** O(n)

### Explanation
- We traverse the array once while calculating the prefix sum.
- The HashMap stores the frequency of previously seen prefix sums.
- For each element, we check whether `prefixSum - k` exists in the HashMap.
- In the worst case, the HashMap can contain up to `n` different prefix sums.
- Therefore, time complexity is **O(n)** and space complexity is **O(n)**.
